      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Harford was settled in 1790 by nine pioneers from Attleborough, Massachusetts, and officially incorporated in 1808.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harford_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first school opened in 1794 at Deacon Tyler's home, followed by a church in 1800 and a library in 1807, laying early community foundations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harford_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An annual Harford Fair began in 1857, celebrating local agriculture and heritage, and still draws regional visitors today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/harford_pennsylvania",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Haverford Township Historical Society, formed in 1939, preserves documents, artifacts, and historic sites like the Lawrence Cabin and Nitre Hall.",
